('q_0816', 'ACCURACY', 'Which sentence correctly uses "fewer" versus "less"?', '["There are less people in the auditorium today.", "There are fewer people in the auditorium today.", "There is fewer water in the reservoir.", "There is less apples in the basket."]'::jsonb, 'There are fewer people in the auditorium today.', 'EASY', 20, 'English', 'Grammar', 'Grammatical Accuracy', '"Fewer" is used for countable nouns (people); "less" is used for uncountable quantities.'),
('q_0817', 'ACCURACY', 'Identify the sentence with correct pronoun case:', '["Between you and I, this decision is final.", "Between you and me, this decision is final.", "Between you and myself, this decision is final.", "Between him and I, this decision is final."]'::jsonb, 'Between you and me, this decision is final.', 'EASY', 20, 'English', 'Grammar', 'Grammatical Accuracy', 'Preposition "between" requires objective case pronouns ("me", not "I").'),
